Notice that 7^4 ≡ 1 mod 5 is significant because it tells us that raising 7 to the power of a multiple of 4 will yield a remainder of 1 when divided by 5. This means we can simplify 7^100 by breaking it down into 7^(4*25), which will also have a remainder of 1 when divided by 5.

